Steps to complete Apple Pay domain verification:

1. Open Stripe Dashboard (live mode):
   https://dashboard.stripe.com/settings/payment_method_domains

2. Click "Add a new domain" → enter: moveleads.cloud
   (Repeat for www.moveleads.cloud if your production deploys to that hostname.)

3. Stripe will display a long string (the merchant-id domain association
   payload). Copy the ENTIRE contents — it should be a single multi-line
   block of base64-looking text.

4. Replace the entire contents of this file with that string. No extra
   whitespace, no trailing newline issues, no quotes around it.

5. Commit + push. Vercel will deploy and serve this file at:
   https://moveleads.cloud/.well-known/apple-developer-merchantid-domain-association

6. Back in Stripe Dashboard, click "Verify". On success, the domain status
   flips to "Verified" and `availablePaymentMethods.applePay` will return
   true on eligible Safari devices.

This file MUST be served as plain text (Content-Type: text/plain) and the
SPA rewrite in vercel.json MUST exclude /.well-known/* — both are already
configured in this commit. Don't change vercel.json's rewrite without
preserving the .well-known exclusion or Apple Pay verification will silently
break again.
